{"purpose":"Definition source for the EKA telemetry event stream: the append-only JSONL record schema and the `eka telemetry` command contract that sto:compliance-telemetry (M5) consumes. It exists so M5 - and any future consumer - aggregates a stable schema without inventing fields, and so implementations agree on the record shape.","content":"# Spec - Telemetry Capture (session event stream)\n\n## 1. Purpose\nDefine the append-only telemetry event stream that makes M5 (sto:compliance-telemetry) derivable, without introducing server-side\nsession state. Session identity is a client-supplied payload value; records are immutable; the store, the corpus and the CKO envelope\nare unchanged.\n\n## 2. Storage and transport\n- One file per session: `docs/telemetry/\u003csessionId\u003e.jsonl` in the repository working tree.\n- `docs/telemetry/*.jsonl` is not `.md`/`.json`, so the existing builder lifts it as a **source-only RSF attachment** (ADR-027); no\n  builder change. A clone receives it via the snapshot; `eka sync pull` caches it in the `attachments` table.\n- Append-only by construction: records are only appended; the file is never rewritten. Each record carries `prevHash` (SHA-256 of the\n  previous record's bytes, `\"\"` for the first), making the chain tamper-evident.\n- `telemetry` is added to the capture transport skip-list so telemetry file names never drive `eka capture` classification.\n\n## 3. Record schema (one JSON object per line, fixed field order)\n```json\n{\"v\":1,\"sessionId\":\"01J...\",\"seq\":3,\"at\":\"2026-11-22T09:14:03Z\",\"repo\":\"eka/eka-cli\",\n \"kind\":\"gate-refusal\",\"subject\":\"eka/sto:compliance-telemetry:1\",\n \"constraint\":\"eka/adr:011-immutable-engineering-knowledge-model\",\n \"gate\":\"transition\",\"reason\":\"transition draft -\u003e approved not in table\",\"prevHash\":\"9f2c...\",\"sessionSource\":\"client\"}\n```\n- `kind` in `constraint-read` | `first-write` | `write` | `gate-refusal` | `gate-pass`.\n- `seq` is a client-maintained monotonic integer per session and is the **only** ordering key. `at` is informational (render/tie-break)\n  and is never used as an ordering or session-boundary key.\n- `subject` / `constraint` are canonical or line forms, or empty when not applicable.\n- `gate` in `conformance` | `transition` | `verify` | `note`; `reason` is the deterministic refusal string from the engine.\n- `sessionSource` in `client` | `env` | `unattributed` - honest degradation, never a fabricated id.\n\n## 4. Command contract\n- `eka telemetry emit --event \u003ckind\u003e --session \u003cid\u003e [--subject \u003cform\u003e] [--constraint \u003cform\u003e] [--gate \u003cid\u003e] [--reason \u003ccode\u003e]`\n  appends one record.\n- `eka telemetry list [--session \u003cid\u003e] [--repo \u003cid\u003e] [--since \u003ct\u003e] [--until \u003ct\u003e] [--json]` returns records sorted by\n  `(sessionId, seq)`, deterministic for a fixed file state.\n- With no `--session`/`EKA_SESSION`, records are written `sessionId:\"\"`, `sessionSource:\"unattributed\"`; no id is synthesized.\n- Auto-emit is opt-in and only runs when a session id is present: publish success -\u003e `first-write`/`write`; conformance block,\n  transition refusal, verify fail -\u003e `gate-refusal`; verify pass -\u003e `gate-pass`. Reads are emitted explicitly by the caller.\n\n## 5. Derivation guarantees (for M5)\n- sessions observed = distinct non-`unattributed` sessionId for repo+period.\n- gate failures = count of `gate-refusal`.\n- read-before-first-write = exists `constraint-read` with `seq` below the session's `first-write` (requires read emission; undercount).\n- repaired-in-session = `gate-refusal` on subject S followed by `gate-pass` on S, same session, increasing `seq` (upper bound).\n\n## 6. Honesty limits (mandatory in any report)\nA report must state: sessions without telemetry, `unattributed` sessions, the telemetry start date (first `docs/telemetry/` commit), and\nthat read coverage is opt-in (so read-before-write is \"\u003e=\" not \"=\"), and that repaired-in-session is a labelled upper bound.\n"}